Description: avcodec/vvc_parser: assemble all picture units of an access unit
 The parser appends a picture unit before testing whether it starts an
 access unit, then outputs at that start. Enhancement-layer pictures
 therefore end up with the next access unit instead of their own.
 .
 Output the preceding access unit before appending a new one's first
 picture unit, as H.266 7.4.2.4.3 requires. Keep the single-layer fast
 path and complete an access unit immediately at the highest VPS layer.
 Otherwise wait for the next access unit or EOF. Queue a second complete
 access unit when a call already produced output.
 .
 Retain the first picture's parameter sets and timestamps until output,
 including when higher layers are absent. Continue internally across a
 buffered picture-unit boundary if there is neither input consumption
 nor an access unit to return.
 .
 VPS_A_3 and OPI_B_3 now produce nine and seventeen correctly grouped
 packets. An OPI_B_3 variant without layer-one TemporalId-four pictures
 also matches the independently determined access-unit boundaries.
 .
